# Blog

Admin-only writing domain (`app/Domain/Blog/`, core). Posts, categories, tags, and editor media. **No public reader surface** — every endpoint is `auth:api` + permission-gated, and the SPA is the only consumer.

- **Sanitization is the security boundary, and it runs before storage.** `PostService` passes `content` through `Purifier::clean($html, 'blog')`; the `blog` profile in `config/purifier.php` is the **single** whitelist, because the SPA renders the stored HTML with `v-html`. Empty/whitespace content sanitizes to `null` (a draft may hold no content). Extend the profile and the SPA Tiptap toolbar **together** — a tag the editor emits but the profile strips is data loss, and a tag the profile allows but the editor never emits is unnecessary attack surface.
- **Slug is generated, and unique against trashed rows too.** `PostService::uniqueSlug` derives from the submitted `slug`, else the `title`, else `post-{random6}`; `slugTaken()` queries `withTrashed()`, so restoring an old post cannot collide with a newer one. Suffixes are `-2`, `-3`, … A title-only update regenerates the slug; an explicit `slug` on update wins.
- **Soft deletes are posts-only.** `blog_posts` is soft-deletable (`trashed` / `restore` endpoints exist); categories, tags, and media rows are hard-deleted. `published_at` is stamped **once**, on the first transition to `published` (create, or update when it is still null) — never overwritten by a later edit.
- **Media rows pin their own disk.** `BlogMediaService` resolves `config('blog.media.disk')` / `media.directory` at upload and stores the disk name on the row; `BlogMedia::url()` reads it back through `Storage::disk($row->disk)`, so changing `BLOG_MEDIA_DISK` later does not break existing URLs. Production/local set `BLOG_MEDIA_DISK=s3ArchivdCe` so URLs come from the public CE bucket **without** a `public/storage` symlink. Allowed mimes (jpg, jpeg, png, gif, webp) and `media.max_size_kb` (4096) are enforced in the request, not the service.
- **Media is never garbage-collected.** Deleting a post does not delete its media rows or objects; `DELETE blog/media/{media}` is the only removal path. Do not add a cascade — an inline image may be shared across drafts.
- **Permissions are two, plus restore.** `view posts` (reads, including `statuses` / `trashed` / a trashed post by id) and `manage posts` (writes across posts, categories, tags, and media). `restore posts` gates `POST blog/posts/{id}/restore` alone. Seeded by `RoleSeeder`; do not add a `manage categories` / `manage tags` split without moving the route groups.
- **Query-mode row actions live in `PostQueryRowActions` / `PostTrashedQueryRowActions`.** Active rows carry `edit` (nav to `blog.posts.edit`) and `delete` (mutate `DELETE blog/posts/{id}`, `manage posts`, confirmation copy `lang/*/list_actions.php` → `delete_post`); trashed rows carry `restore`. Contract: [list-display-modes.md](../../docs/platform/list-display-modes.md).
- **Menu + route names are pinned.** Sidebar `blog.posts.index` parent with Posts / Categories / Tags children, roles Root/Admin/Moderator/Management; `blog.posts.trashed` is a registered SPA route reachable from the Posts view, **not** a menu child. `MenuSeeder` + `MenuSeederTest` pin the tree, `MenuSeederConformanceTest` pins conformance, and `config/spa-routes.php` holds the names.
- UUID primary keys on every table; `blog_posts.status` is the `PostStatus` enum (`draft` / `published`); `featured_media_id` is nullable.

Detail: [docs/domains/blog/README.md](../../docs/domains/blog/README.md). Tests: `BlogPostApiTest`, `MenuSeederTest`, `MenuSeederConformanceTest`.
